                "retweet_count": 14,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "More than $193 million announced today to help transform Pennsylvania\u2019s rural healthcare! I was proud to vote for the Working Families Tax Cut Act that made this investment possible. Visiting Pennsylvania\u2019s  Wyoming County Healthcare Center and Guthrie Robert Packer Hospital in Sayre, I saw firsthand how deeply these communities rely on their rural health care facilities. Families shouldn\u2019t have to drive long distances for high-quality care, and this funding will help expand access, strengthen the rural health workforce, and modernize facilities so care is available where it\u2019s needed most.",
